{number: 70}
{title: Take My Life, and Let It Be}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Take my life, and let it be
Consecrated, [G7] Lord, to [C] Thee;
Take my moments and my [F] days;
Let them [C] flow in [G7] ceaseless [C] praise.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Take my hands, and let them move
At the impulse [G7] of Thy [C] love;
Take my feet, and let them [F] be
Swift and [C] beautiful [G7] for [C] Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Take my voice, and let me sing
Always, only, [G7] for my [C] King;
Take my lips, and let them [F] be
Filled with [C] messages [G7] from [C] Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[C] Take my will, and make it Thine;
It shall be no [G7] longer [C] mine;
Take my heart, it is Thine [F] own;
It shall [C] be Thy [G7] royal [C] throne.
{end_of_verse}
